## Move Registry → Developer/API to Settings

Context: The interactive API explorer belonged under Settings with other
developer tooling, not under Registry domain management. Moved the whole
Developer sidebar group (API) from Registry into Settings.

Changes:

1. `src/front/config/menu_config.json`
   Removed Registry `registry-developer` group; added Settings
   `settings-developer` → API.
2. `src/front/templates/registry.html`
   Dropped api-section include and query-api CSS/JS assets.
3. `src/front/templates/settings.html`
   Added api-section plus query-api CSS/JS (available to all roles).
4. `src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_api.html` (new)
   Settings wrapper around the shared query-api partial.
5. `src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_api.html`
   Deleted — replaced by the Settings partial.
6. `tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py`
   Assert API endpoint cards live on `/settings`, not `/registry/`.
7. `docs/development.md`
   Smoke-check table updated for the new API location.

Modified files:
- src/front/config/menu_config.json
- src/front/templates/registry.html
- src/front/templates/settings.html
- src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_api.html
- src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_api.html (deleted)
- tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py
- docs/development.md

