## Move Registry → Automation to Settings

Context: Scheduler and Build Analytics sat under Registry even though
their APIs already live under `/settings/*`. Moved the whole Automation
sidebar group into Settings alongside Developer tooling.

Changes:

1. `src/front/config/menu_config.json`
   Removed Registry `registry-automation`; added Settings
   `settings-automation` (Scheduler, Build Analytics) before Developer.
2. `src/front/templates/registry.html`
   Dropped schedule / build-analytics sections and their JS assets.
3. `src/front/templates/settings.html`
   Hosts both automation sections; loads `schedule.js` and
   `build-analytics.js` for all roles.
4. `src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_schedule.html` (new)
   Moved from registry partial; comment updated.
5. `src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_build_analytics.html` (new)
   Moved from registry partial; comment updated.
6. `src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_schedule.html` +
   `_registry_build_analytics.html`
   Deleted after the move.
7. `src/front/static/config/js/build-analytics.js`
   Comment / guard wording now refer to Settings Automation.
8. `tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py`
   Assert schedule + build analytics live on `/settings`.
9. `docs/development.md` + `docs/code_organization.md` + `docs/data-access.md`
   Location references updated.

