## Move Registry Teams to Settings Admin

Context: Per-domain team role assignments are an administrative concern.
The Teams matrix was therefore moved from Registry into Settings → Admin,
alongside app permissions and other administrator-only controls.

Changes:

1. `src/front/config/menu_config.json`
   Moved the admin-only Teams item from Registry Domains to Settings Admin.
2. `src/front/templates/registry.html`
   Removed the Teams section and its page-specific assets from Registry.
3. `src/front/templates/settings.html`
   Added the admin-only Teams section and loaded its CSS/JavaScript assets.
4. `src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_teams.html`
   Added the Teams matrix partial in its new Settings location.
5. `src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_teams.html`
   Deleted the obsolete Registry partial.
6. `src/front/static/registry/js/registry-teams.js` and
   `src/front/static/registry/css/registry-teams.css`
   Updated module comments for the new Settings → Admin location.
7. `src/front/static/config/js/permissions.js`,
   `src/front/static/domain/js/domain-review.js`,
   `src/front/routes/home.py`, and `src/front/templates/access_denied.html`
   Updated user guidance to Settings → Admin → Teams.
8. `src/api/routers/internal/settings.py`,
   `src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py`,
   `src/back/objects/registry/ReviewService.py`, and
   `tests/units/registry/test_review_service.py`
   Updated internal documentation references without changing contracts.
9. `tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py`
   Added coverage proving Teams renders in Settings and not Registry.
10. `docs/development.md` and `docs/code_organization.md`
    Updated page ownership documentation.

